oelemento/federated-ehr-fm,0,0,other,federated-ehr-fm-research-license,LICENSE,false,"Research checkpoints accompanying *Multi-Hospital Electronic Health Record Foundation Models Without Pooling Patient Data: A Comparison of Federated Learning and Inference-Time Ensembling* (O. Elemento, Weill Cornell Medicine). **Research artifact — not a medical device; not cleared or approved for clinical use.**",noassertion,yes,LICENSE,LICENSE,full,file_only,"Federated EHR FM Research License Copyright (c) 2026 Olivier Elemento, Weill Cornell Medicine. These model checkpoints are derivative works of credentialed intensive-care datasets (MIMIC-IV, eICU-CRD, and HiRID via PhysioNet; SICdb). They are released for non-commercial academic research only, under the following terms: 1. Eligibility. You must already hold the relevant credentialed-access approvals for the source datasets (PhysioNet credentialing for MIMIC-IV/eICU/HiRID; SICdb access) and remain bound by those data-use agreements. 2. Permitted use. Reproduction and verification of the accompanying manuscript and non-commercial methodological research on multi-institutional EHR modeling. 3. Prohibited use. Redistribution of the weights; any attempt to re-identify individuals; clinical or diagnostic deployment; commercial use; and any use that violates the source datasets' data-use agreements. 4. No warranty. Provided ""as is"", without warranty of any kind. This is a research artifact and is not a medical device. Access is granted on a per-application basis at the authors' discretion.",license_other_raw/oelemento/federated-ehr-fm/LICENSE,tag
