NoeFlandre/GPT2-From-Scratch,0,0,odc-by,,,false,"A GPT-2-style transformer implemented in PyTorch. `model.safetensors` contains float32 weights from training step 19,072.",noassertion,yes,LICENSE,LICENSE,full,file_only,ODC-By 1.0 applies to the model weights in `model.safetensors`. Full license text: https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/by/1-0/ Training data attribution: FineWeb-Edu sample-10BT https://huggingface.co/datasets/HuggingFaceFW/fineweb-edu FineWeb-Edu is separately released under ODC-By 1.0 and is subject to Common Crawl's Terms of Use: https://commoncrawl.org/terms-of-use The source code is MIT-licensed: https://github.com/NoeFlandre/GPT2-From-Scratch/blob/e7282bef17e43eb1ce74859469b3446b8ed274dd/LICENSE,,tag
google/electra-base-discriminator,41852016,215,apache-2.0,,,false,"**ELECTRA** is a new method for self-supervised language representation learning. It can be used to pre-train transformer networks using relatively little compute. ELECTRA models are trained to distinguish ""real"" input tokens vs ""fake"" input tokens generated by another neural network, similar to the discriminator of a [GAN](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1406.2661.pdf). At small scale, ELECTRA achieves strong results even when trained on a single GPU. At large scale, ELECTRA achieves state-of-the-art results on the [SQuAD 2.0](https://rajpurkar.github.io/SQuAD-explorer/) dataset.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
facebook/wav2vec2-base,2062455,136,apache-2.0,,,false,The base model pretrained on 16kHz sampled speech audio. When using the model make sure that your speech input is also sampled at 16Khz.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
nlpaueb/legal-bert-base-uncased,1099117,330,cc-by-sa-4.0,,,false,"LEGAL-BERT is a family of BERT models for the legal domain, intended to assist legal NLP research, computational law, and legal technology applications. To pre-train the different variations of LEGAL-BERT, we collected 12 GB of diverse English legal text from several fields (e.g., legislation, court cases, contracts) scraped from publicly available resources. Sub-domain variants (CONTRACTS-, EURLEX-, ECHR-) and/or general LEGAL-BERT perform better than using BERT out of the box for domain-specific tasks. A light-weight model (33% the size of BERT-BASE) pre-trained from scratch on legal data with competitive performance is also available. <br/><br/>",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
google/fnet-base,505159,21,apache-2.0,,,false,Pretrained model on English language using a masked language modeling (MLM) and next sentence prediction (NSP) objective. It was introduced in [this paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2105.03824) and first released in [this repository](https://github.com/google-research/google-research/tree/master/f_net). This model is cased: it makes a difference between english and English. The model achieves 0.58 accuracy on MLM objective and 0.80 on NSP objective.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
MCG-NJU/videomae-base,372808,59,cc-by-nc-4.0,,,false,VideoMAE model pre-trained on Kinetics-400 for 1600 epochs in a self-supervised way. It was introduced in the paper [VideoMAE: Masked Autoencoders are Data-Efficient Learners for Self-Supervised Video Pre-Training](https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.12602) by Tong et al. and first released in [this repository](https://github.com/MCG-NJU/VideoMAE).,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
mistralai/Mistral-7B-v0.1,325248,4222,apache-2.0,,,false,The Mistral-7B-v0.1 Large Language Model (LLM) is a pretrained generative text model with 7 billion parameters. Mistral-7B-v0.1 outperforms Llama 2 13B on all benchmarks we tested.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
cointegrated/rubert-tiny2,283488,183,mit,,,false,This is an updated version of [cointegrated/rubert-tiny](https://huggingface.co/cointegrated/rubert-tiny): a small Russian BERT-based encoder with high-quality sentence embeddings. This [post in Russian](https://habr.com/ru/post/669674/) gives more details.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
facebook/wav2vec2-xls-r-300m,281767,142,apache-2.0,,,false,[Facebook's Wav2Vec2 XLS-R](https://ai.facebook.com/blog/wav2vec-20-learning-the-structure-of-speech-from-raw-audio/) counting **300 million** parameters.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
google/electra-small-discriminator,194518,45,apache-2.0,,,false,"**ELECTRA** is a new method for self-supervised language representation learning. It can be used to pre-train transformer networks using relatively little compute. ELECTRA models are trained to distinguish ""real"" input tokens vs ""fake"" input tokens generated by another neural network, similar to the discriminator of a [GAN](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1406.2661.pdf). At small scale, ELECTRA achieves strong results even when trained on a single GPU. At large scale, ELECTRA achieves state-of-the-art results on the [SQuAD 2.0](https://rajpurkar.github.io/SQuAD-explorer/) dataset.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
MaziyarPanahi/Mistral-7B-v0.1-GGUF,155461,0,apache-2.0,,,false,- Model creator: [mistralai](https://huggingface.co/mistralai) - Original model: [mistralai/Mistral-7B-v0.1](https://huggingface.co/mistralai/Mistral-7B-v0.1),yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
openvla/openvla-7b,152456,263,mit,,,false,"OpenVLA 7B (`openvla-7b`) is an open vision-language-action model trained on 970K robot manipulation episodes from the [Open X-Embodiment](https://robotics-transformer-x.github.io/) dataset. The model takes language instructions and camera images as input and generates robot actions. It supports controlling multiple robots out-of-the-box, and can be quickly adapted for new robot domains via (parameter-efficient) fine-tuning.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
facebook/wav2vec2-xls-r-1b,129725,39,apache-2.0,,,false,[Facebook's Wav2Vec2 XLS-R](https://ai.facebook.com/blog/xls-r-self-supervised-speech-processing-for-128-languages) counting **1 billion** parameters.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
google/mobilebert-uncased,126756,79,apache-2.0,,,false,"MobileBERT is a thin version of BERT_LARGE, while equipped with bottleneck structures and a carefully designed balance between self-attentions and feed-forward networks.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
tohoku-nlp/bert-base-japanese-char-v3,119679,11,apache-2.0,,,false,This is a [BERT](https://github.com/google-research/bert) model pretrained on texts in the Japanese language.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
google/bigbird-roberta-base,117970,66,apache-2.0,,,false,"BigBird, is a sparse-attention based transformer which extends Transformer based models, such as BERT to much longer sequences. Moreover, BigBird comes along with a theoretical understanding of the capabilities of a complete transformer that the sparse model can handle.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
nlpaueb/sec-bert-base,112588,36,cc-by-sa-4.0,,,false,"<div style=""text-align: justify"">",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
facebook/wav2vec2-large-xlsr-53,108246,166,apache-2.0,,,false,"The base model pretrained on 16kHz sampled speech audio. When using the model make sure that your speech input is also sampled at 16Khz. Note that this model should be fine-tuned on a downstream task, like Automatic Speech Recognition. Check out [this blog](https://huggingface.co/blog/fine-tune-wav2vec2-english) for more information.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
krpraveen/sanskrit-en-custom-transformer,92287,0,mit,,,false,"A compact encoder–decoder Transformer trained **from scratch** on 10,000 Sanskrit–English pairs (NLU Assignment 2), with a joint SentencePiece BPE vocabulary. It is small and fast — meant to be efficient rather than to match large pretrained models. This is **not** a 🤗 Transformers architecture, so it ships with a self-contained `modeling.py`.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
sergeyzh/rubert-tiny-turbo,77891,31,mit,,,false,language: - ru,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
tohoku-nlp/bert-large-japanese-v2,66731,14,apache-2.0,,,false,This is a [BERT](https://github.com/google-research/bert) model pretrained on texts in the Japanese language.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
google/electra-large-discriminator,59769,23,apache-2.0,,,false,"**ELECTRA** is a new method for self-supervised language representation learning. It can be used to pre-train transformer networks using relatively little compute. ELECTRA models are trained to distinguish ""real"" input tokens vs ""fake"" input tokens generated by another neural network, similar to the discriminator of a [GAN](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1406.2661.pdf). At small scale, ELECTRA achieves strong results even when trained on a single GPU. At large scale, ELECTRA achieves state-of-the-art results on the [SQuAD 2.0](https://rajpurkar.github.io/SQuAD-explorer/) dataset.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
tohoku-nlp/bert-base-japanese-v3,41596,65,apache-2.0,,,false,This is a [BERT](https://github.com/google-research/bert) model pretrained on texts in the Japanese language.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
facebook/wav2vec2-large-es-voxpopuli,40361,3,cc-by-nc-4.0,,,false,[Facebook's Wav2Vec2](https://ai.facebook.com/blog/wav2vec-20-learning-the-structure-of-speech-from-raw-audio/) large model pretrained on the es unlabeled subset of [VoxPopuli corpus](https://arxiv.org/abs/2101.00390).,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
facebook/vit-mae-base,37615,43,apache-2.0,,,false,"Vision Transformer (ViT) model pre-trained using the MAE method. It was introduced in the paper [Masked Autoencoders Are Scalable Vision Learners](https://arxiv.org/abs/2111.06377) by Kaiming He, Xinlei Chen, Saining Xie, Yanghao Li, Piotr Dollár, Ross Girshick and first released in [this repository](https://github.com/facebookresearch/mae).",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
facebook/flava-full,35542,45,bsd-3-clause,,,false,"FLAVA model was developed by the researchers at FAIR to understand if a single model can work across different modalities with a unified architecture. The model was pretrained solely using publicly available multimodal datasets containing 70M image-text pairs in total and thus fully reproducible. Unimodal datasets ImageNet and BookCorpus + CCNews were also used to provide unimodal data to the model. The model (i) similar to CLIP can be used for arbitrary image classification tasks in a zero-shot manner (ii) used for image or text retrieval in a zero-shot manner (iii) can also be fine-tuned for natural language understanding (NLU) tasks such as GLUE and vision-and-language reasoning tasks such as VQA v2. The model is able to use the data available as images, text corpus and image-text pairs",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
vidore/colqwen2-v1.0-hf,31843,23,apache-2.0,,,false,"> [!IMPORTANT] > This version of ColQwen2 should be loaded with the `transformers 🤗` release or [Sentence Transformers](https://www.sbert.net/), not with `colpali-engine`. > It was converted using the `convert_colqwen2_weights_to_hf.py` script > from the [`vidore/colqwen2-v1.0-merged`](https://huggingface.co/vidore/colqwen2-v1.0-merged) checkpoint.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
TencentGameMate/chinese-wav2vec2-base,29717,66,mit,,,false,Pretrained on 10k hours WenetSpeech L subset. More details in [TencentGameMate/chinese_speech_pretrain](https://github.com/TencentGameMate/chinese_speech_pretrain),yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
sergeyzh/BERTA,28375,40,mit,,,false,"Модель для расчетов эмбеддингов предложений на русском и английском языках получена методом дистилляции эмбеддингов [ai-forever/FRIDA](https://huggingface.co/ai-forever/FRIDA) (размер эмбеддингов - 1536, слоёв - 24) в [sergeyzh/LaBSE-ru-turbo](https://huggingface.co/sergeyzh/LaBSE-ru-turbo) (размер эмбеддингов - 768, слоёв - 12). Основной режим использования FRIDA - CLS pooling заменен на mean pooling. Каких-либо других изменений поведения модели не производилось. Дистиляция выполнена в максимально возможном объеме - эмбеддинги русских и английских предложений, работа префиксов.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
facebook/mms-300m,26547,221,cc-by-nc-4.0,,,false,Facebook's MMS counting *300m* parameters.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
mlinslab/neurovfm-encoder,26094,36,cc-by-nc-sa-4.0,,,false,[**Paper**](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41591-026-04497-1) / [**Interactive Demo**](https://neurovfm.mlins.org) / [**GitHub**](https://github.com/MLNeurosurg/neurovfm) /,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
hotdogs/Qwen3.8-27B-abliterated-cyber-preview-MTP-GGUF,19473,7,apache-2.0,,,false,"GGUF builds of the **offensive-security / agentic tool-calling** merged model (the cyber LoRA merged into the abliterated base at **scale 1.0**, with the **MTP head preserved**). All files are imatrix-quantized and are ready to run in [llama.cpp](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp) with native **self-speculative (MTP) decoding**.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
TheBloke/Mistral-7B-v0.1-GGUF,18233,279,apache-2.0,,,false,"<!-- header start --> <!-- 200823 --> <div style=""width: auto; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto""> </div> <div style=""display: flex; justify-content: space-between; width: 100%;""> <div style=""display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start;""> <p style=""margin-top: 0.5em; margin-bottom: 0em;""><a href=""https://discord.gg/theblokeai"">Chat & support: TheBloke's Discord server</a></p> </div> <div style=""display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-end;""> <p style=""margin-top: 0.5em; margin-bottom: 0em;""><a href=""https://www.patreon.com/TheBlokeAI"">Want to contribute? TheBloke's Patreon page</a></p> </div> </div> <div style=""text-align:center; margin-top: 0em; margin-bottom: 0em""><p style=""margin-top: 0.25em; margin-bottom: 0em;"">TheBloke's LLM work is generously s",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
jonfd/electra-small-nordic,15625,4,cc-by-4.0,,,false,"This model was pretrained on the following corpora: * The [Icelandic Gigaword Corpus](http://igc.arnastofnun.is/) (IGC) * The Icelandic Common Crawl Corpus (IC3) * The [Icelandic Crawled Corpus](https://huggingface.co/datasets/jonfd/ICC) (ICC) * The [Multilingual Colossal Clean Crawled Corpus](https://huggingface.co/datasets/mc4) (mC4) - Icelandic, Norwegian, Swedish and Danish text obtained from .is, .no, .se and .dk domains, respectively",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
sergeyzh/rubert-tiny-lite,15230,1,mit,,,false,"Быстрая модель BERT для русского языка с размером ембеддинга 256 и длиной контекста 512. Модель получена методом последовательной дистилляции моделей [sergeyzh/rubert-tiny-turbo](https://huggingface.co/sergeyzh/rubert-tiny-turbo) и [BAAI/bge-m3](https://huggingface.co/BAAI/bge-m3). Выигрывает по скорости у [rubert-tiny-turbo](https://huggingface.co/sergeyzh/rubert-tiny-turbo) при аналогичном качестве на CPU в ~x1.4, на GPU в ~x1.2 раза.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
facebook/wav2vec2-conformer-rel-pos-large,14944,12,apache-2.0,,,false,"Wav2Vec2 Conformer with relative position embeddings, pretrained on 960 hours of Librispeech on 16kHz sampled speech audio. When using the model make sure that your speech input is also sampled at 16Khz.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
nguyenvulebinh/wav2vec2-base-vi,13789,10,cc-by-nc-4.0,,,false,We use wav2vec2 architecture for doing Self-Supervised learning,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
facebook/wav2vec2-large,12444,13,apache-2.0,,,false,"The base model pretrained on 16kHz sampled speech audio. When using the model make sure that your speech input is also sampled at 16Khz. Note that this model should be fine-tuned on a downstream task, like Automatic Speech Recognition. Check out [this blog](https://huggingface.co/blog/fine-tune-wav2vec2-english) for more information.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
vidore/colpali-v1.3-hf,12285,27,gemma,,,false,"> [!IMPORTANT] > This version of ColPali should be loaded with the `transformers 🤗` release or [Sentence Transformers](https://www.sbert.net/), not with `colpali-engine`. > It was converted using the [`convert_colpali_weights_to_hf.py` script](https://github.com/tonywu71/transformers/blob/21c1309637aee97ca4fb8eb3b31830913a0f99a5/src/transformers/models/colpali/convert_colpali_weights_to_hf.py) > from the [`vidore/colpali-v1.3-merged`](https://huggingface.co/vidore/colpali-v1.3-merged) checkpoint.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
