whoashish115/Moonfrost-777M,365,1,apache-2.0,,,false,**[Code](https://github.com/whoashish115/moonfrost-ai)** &middot; **[Site](https://moonfrost-ai.vercel.app)** &middot; **[Training runs](https://wandb.ai/whoashish115-base/moonfrost-777m)**,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
MIC-DKFZ/nnFoundationViT,361,18,cc-by-sa-4.0,,,false,<sub>Copyright German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ) and contributors. Please make sure that your usage of these models is in compliance with their license.<sub>,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
capemox/ettin-encoder-32m-pretrain-50m,361,3,apache-2.0,,,false,A retrieval encoder pretrained from [jhu-clsp/ettin-encoder-32m](https://huggingface.co/jhu-clsp/ettin-encoder-32m) on **a 50M-pair balanced split of the DenseOn embeddings pre-training dataset**.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Compactbot/catgirl-1m,361,1,apache-2.0,,,false,"A **1,064,737-parameter** tsundere-catgirl conversational persona model. A full fine-tune of the community's [Glint-2](https://huggingface.co/Glint-Research/Glint-2) looped-block base, trained on a ~216 KB synthetic `User:`/`Cat:` dialogue corpus of tsundere-catgirl chatter.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Crawlnet/queen-v6,361,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"A small language model trained **from scratch**. **Pretraining data: pages the Crawlnet crawlers read on the crypto web** (real browsers; 65% of the tokens trained), **public market, funding and on-chain records written out as plain-text pages** (4%), **study notes a general-purpose LLM wrote for 153,245 of those pages** (24%) and **question/answer pairs a general-purpose LLM generated from those pages** (7%); details in Pretraining data below. **Tokenizer: trained on this dataset's pages only (crawler pages and record pages).** No pretrained weights, no FineWeb, no other corpus. **Chat tuning: question/answer pairs generated by a general-purpose LLM from those pages (with the study notes' own Q&A), pairs cut from the pages and open-book conversations that answer from retrieved pages with",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
C-a-Star-Technology-Official/StarO-AI-2.69-Super,360,4,creativeml-openrail-m,,,false,"<svg version=""1.3"" width=""300.000000pt"" height=""100.000000pt"" viewBox=""0 0 925.000000 255.000000"" preserveAspectRatio=""xMidYMid meet""> <metadata id=""metadata1""> Created by Hawa-Al-Akram, Update By C.a. Star </metadata> <g transform=""translate(0.000000,277.000000) scale(0.100000,-0.100000)"" fill=""#FFFFFF"" stroke=""none"" id=""g7""> <path d=""m 1310,2193 c -279,-37 -433,-240 -360,-475 50,-161 148,-226 475,-313 173,-45 235,-92 235,-178 0,-141 -167,-213 -400,-173 -104,18 -175,39 -232,68 l -38,18 v -119 c 0,-111 2,-121 20,-131 40,-21 176,-50 273,-58 284,-23 492,56 583,220 27,50 29,60 29,168 0,108 -2,118 -29,168 -72,129 -179,191 -458,262 -170,44 -233,93 -233,180 0,57 26,92 90,121 109,49 324,26 473,-50 l 42,-21 v 124 124 l -47,15 c -106,34 -174,47 -278,51 -61,2 -126,2 -145,-1 z"" id=""path1""></path> <pa",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
wayneworkman2012/peacebell-v1-291M,360,2,apache-2.0,,,false,"**Peacebell** is a **291M-parameter** GPT-style decoder trained **from scratch** to know the history of World War II: custom architecture, a custom 28,000-token SentencePiece vocabulary, and a 32,768-token context. It is not a fine-tune of any other model and was not distilled from one. The weights started random, and every token it saw in training came from the datasets listed under ""Datasets used to train.""",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
mradermacher/JugnuLM-110M-GGUF,359,0,apache-2.0,,,false,<!-- ### quantize_version: 2 --> <!-- ### output_tensor_quantised: 1 --> <!-- ### convert_type: hf --> <!-- ### vocab_type: --> <!-- ### tags: --> <!-- ### quants: x-f16 Q4_K_S Q2_K Q8_0 Q6_K Q3_K_M Q3_K_S Q3_K_L Q4_K_M Q5_K_S Q5_K_M IQ4_XS --> <!-- ### quants_skip: --> <!-- ### skip_mmproj: --> static quants of https://huggingface.co/altslate/JugnuLM-110M,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
AwaisAdilKhokhar/ravaan-ar-70m,359,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"70M parameters, trained from scratch on a purpose-built 85.4M-token Urdu corpus. On its own terms it is a competent small Urdu language model. **Its reason for existing is to be the matched baseline** for [`ravaan-diff-70m`](https://huggingface.co/AwaisAdilKhokhar/ravaan-diff-70m) — identical corpus, identical model, identical task mixture and tokenizer, so that the two can be compared without confounds.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
EleutherAI/deep-ignorance-pretraining-stage-strong-filter,358,1,apache-2.0,,,false,This model suite is presented in the paper [Deep Ignorance: Filtering Pretraining Data Builds Tamper-Resistant Safeguards into Open-Weight LLMs](https://huggingface.co/papers/2508.06601). **Project Page**: https://deepignorance.ai/ **Code**: https://github.com/EleutherAI/deep-ignorance,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
AneekC/quipu-114m,357,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"A 114,114,048-parameter language model trained from scratch on a single 8 GB laptop GPU (RTX 5060 Laptop): own weights, own data pipeline, no fine-tuned base.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
flaviussteff/base-ro-125m,353,0,mit,,,false,"`Base-Ro-125M` is a 124.8M-parameter causal language model based on the modern **LLaMA architecture**, trained **from scratch (""Token Zero"")** purely on Romanian web text.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
VADRK155/Cortex-1-Code,352,1,mit,,,false,"A small GPT model for code generation, trained completely from scratch (custom PyTorch architecture, no `transformers` library involved).",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
thebajajra/RexReranker-0.6B,349,10,apache-2.0,,,false,"<p align=""center""> </p> <p align=""center""> </p>",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
dicta-il/DictaLM-3.0-1.7B-Thinking-GGUF,348,3,apache-2.0,,,false,"Dicta-LM 3.0 is a powerful open-weight collection of LLMs, trained on extensive corpora of Hebrew and English texts. The models are available for download and for unlimited use. The models set a new SOTA for their weight-class for Hebrew, both as base models and chat models.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Compactbot/hypernix-3.1-mini,348,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"Pretraining continuation of [ray0rf1re/HyperNix.3-mini](https://huggingface.co/ray0rf1re/HyperNix.3-mini), trained by @Compactbot on behalf of the model-requests board (#9).",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
davemaxuellkr/scglm-v2-46m,347,0,mit,,,false,"SCG-LM V2 is a **46,346,752-parameter** Llama-style language model trained **from random initialization** on **45.0 billion tokens** of human-written English. Training took 31.9 hours on a single H100. It is a **base model**: it continues text, and it has not been instruction-tuned or safety-tuned. It was built for Track 01 of the Global Innovation Build Challenge V2 (train a language model from scratch with at most 50M parameters).",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
VertexResearch/Vertex-0.6-200M-Base,345,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"A 198M-parameter decoder-only transformer (Qwen3 architecture), pretrained from scratch by Vertex Research on 20B tokens of filtered English web text (Ultra-FineWeb). It is the largest model in the Vertex 0.6 family and the strongest base we have trained so far. Apache 2.0, weights and tokenizer included.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
SupraLabs/Supra2-Nano,345,23,apache-2.0,,,false,"<h1 align=""center"">Supra2-Nano</h1>",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
AwaisAdilKhokhar/ravaan-diff-70m,343,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"**To our knowledge this is the first masked diffusion language model trained for Urdu** (literature searched 2026-09-23; see *Novelty* below for what that claim does and does not cover). 70M parameters, trained from scratch on a purpose-built 85.4M-token Urdu corpus.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
google/multiberts-seed_1,342,2,apache-2.0,,,false,"MultiBERTs is a collection of checkpoints and a statistical library to support robust research on BERT. We provide 25 BERT-base models trained with similar hyper-parameters as [the original BERT model](https://github.com/google-research/bert) but with different random seeds, which causes variations in the initial weights and order of training instances. The aim is to distinguish findings that apply to a specific artifact (i.e., a particular instance of the model) from those that apply to the more general procedure.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
davemaxuellkr/Global-Innovation-Build-Challenge-V2,340,0,mit,,,false,"SCG-LM V2.1 is a **46,346,752-parameter** Llama-style language model trained **from random initialization**. It is our [SCG-LM V2](https://huggingface.co/davemaxuellkr/scglm-v2-46m) base model, pretrained on 45.0 billion tokens of human-written English, with one more short training stage. That stage fine-tuned it for 20 minutes on the **training splits** of the four benchmarks it is evaluated on: HellaSwag, ARC, PIQA and WinoGrande. It was built for Track 01 of the Global Innovation Build Challenge V2 (train a language model from scratch with at most 50M parameters). No pretrained weights from any other model and no distillation were used.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
OPENGCM/GTM-v2-chat,339,4,apache-2.0,,,false,"A ~120M parameter, decoder-only GPT-style model, base-pretrained from scratch and then fine-tuned (SFT) on UltraChat to behave like a chat assistant. Single RTX Pro 6000, ~4.16B pretraining tokens + ~1B SFT tokens.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
vijaymohan/gpt2-tinystories-from-scratch-10m,337,1,mit,,,false,"This repository contains a GPT-2–style language model trained from scratch on the [roneneldan/TinyStories](https://huggingface.co/datasets/roneneldan/TinyStories) dataset using Hugging Face’s Transformers library on Google Colab Pro+ A100 GPU. The training objective was to build a small, educational, and easily reproducible transformer LM for story generation.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
edededdy/ShallowSeek-mini-it,337,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"`ShallowSeek-mini-it` is the **instruction-tuned (chat) version of [ShallowSeek-mini-base](https://huggingface.co/edededdy/ShallowSeek-mini-base)**, a tiny DeepSeek-V3-style Mixture-of-Experts model trained from scratch on a laptop CPU. It has **11.0M parameters**, of which **6.3M are active per token**.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
robotics-diffusion-transformer/rdt-1b,334,106,mit,,,false,"RDT-1B is a 1B-parameter imitation learning Diffusion Transformer pre-trained on 1M+ multi-robot episodes. Given language instruction and RGB images of up to three views, RDT can predict the next 64 robot actions. RDT is compatible with almost all modern mobile manipulators, from single-arm to dual-arm, joint to EEF, position to velocity, and even wheeled locomotion.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
OPENGCM/GTM-3-base,334,8,apache-2.0,,,false,"A ~75M parameter, decoder-only GPT-style **base** language model, trained from scratch on a single RTX Pro 6000, using RoPE (rotary position embeddings)",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Diamegs/PIT-4B-202412,333,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"**Point-In-Time (PIT)** is a family of GPT-style language models trained on chronologically-ordered monthly snapshots of [FineWeb](https://huggingface.co/datasets/HuggingFaceFW/fineweb). Each checkpoint captures the state of knowledge available up to a specific month, making them suitable for temporal reasoning and point-in-time analysis tasks.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
IvmeLabs/Ivme-Conversate-v2-Base,333,5,apache-2.0,,,false,"**İvme** (Turkish: *acceleration*) is a series of stupidly small language models built to punch above their weight. This is the second release: a 24M parameter decoder-only base model trained from scratch, this time with a much heavier training diet.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
AlfredQin/sonobase,330,0,cc-by-nc-4.0,,,false,**Paper:** [arXiv:2609.19230](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.19230) · **Code:** [github.com/AlfredQin/sonobase](https://github.com/AlfredQin/sonobase) · **Data manifest:** [10.5281/zenodo.22770825](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22770825) · **Demo:** [Hugging Face Space](https://huggingface.co/spaces/AlfredQin/sonobase-demo) · **Website:** [alfredqin.github.io/sonobase-web](https://alfredqin.github.io/sonobase-web/),yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
