MinimaLabs/KeyLM-75M,259,18,apache-2.0,,,false,"KeyLM-75M is a 75M parameter base language model trained from scratch on approximately 18 billion tokens. That training budget is a small fraction of what comparable small models use (SmolLM-135M was trained on roughly 600B tokens, SmolLM2-135M on roughly 2T).",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
mokshjain/pico,259,0,mit,,,false,"**Pico** is a **48.2M-parameter** decoder-only transformer trained from scratch in pure JAX (no Flax, no optax), following Karpathy's [nanochat](https://github.com/karpathy/nanochat) recipe and extending it to build a complete **tool-calling agent** from pretraining through on-policy reinforcement learning—without any distillation or synthetic LLM-generated data.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
MaziyarPanahi/typhoon-7b-GGUF,258,1,apache-2.0,,,false,- Model creator: [scb10x](https://huggingface.co/scb10x) - Original model: [scb10x/typhoon-7b](https://huggingface.co/scb10x/typhoon-7b),yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
mys/timesfm-3.0-GGUF,258,1,apache-2.0,,,false,"**Google TimesFM 3.0** foundation time-series forecaster compiled from (20 mixing layers, 1280 hidden, patch 32→64).",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
thebajajra/RexBERT-base,257,11,apache-2.0,,,false,"> **TL;DR**: An encoder-only transformer (ModernBERT-style) for **e-commerce** applications, trained in three phases—**Pre-training**, **Context Extension**, and **Decay**—to power product search, attribute extraction, classification, and embeddings use cases. The model has been trained on 2.3T+ tokens along with 350B+ e-commerce-specific tokens",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
izumi-lab/electra-small-japanese-fin-discriminator,256,0,cc-by-sa-4.0,,,false,This is a [ELECTRA](https://github.com/google-research/electra) model pretrained on texts in the Japanese language.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Compactbot/swordies-22m,256,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"**A 22.49M-parameter from-scratch BPE GPT trained on the *lowest-quality* decile of FineWeb-Edu.** This is a **data-quality ablation**, not a usable language model. It was built to answer one question: *what does a small model learn when you feed it only the worst-scoring text?*",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Diamegs/PIT-4B-201912,255,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"**Point-In-Time (PIT)** is a family of GPT-style language models trained on chronologically-ordered monthly snapshots of [FineWeb](https://huggingface.co/datasets/HuggingFaceFW/fineweb). Each checkpoint captures the state of knowledge available up to a specific month, making them suitable for temporal reasoning and point-in-time analysis tasks.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Ilides/cortex-0.3-0.02b,255,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"**GPT conversacional de 20,6M parámetros, entrenado desde cero en NumPy puro** (sin PyTorch durante el entrenamiento) sobre un corpus bilingüe ES/EN de 473M tokens y afinado en español para conversación.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
0v0ai/0u0-pelican-pro-0.2B-GGUF,255,2,apache-2.0,,,false,"<div align=""center"">",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
