mondk/Msh-Tiny-14M,228,3,apache-2.0,,,false,"hi guys, im lazy to write, so this was written by claude, ty",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
aquas-modela/Aqua-1.0.0,228,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"Aqua is a 100-million-parameter model trained on vast amounts of curated, organized data. It is designed for general-purpose responses and is retrained daily. Its intended use is as a base model for fine-tuning by companies or individuals, and it is released under the Apache 2.0 license for flexible use. Although this version has been trained on highly refined data up to 2026, it is the smallest variant. We will soon launch Aqua-3.0.0, a model optimized for more fluent Spanish conversations, with future plans to add support for English, Chinese, Arabic, and Russian.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Diamegs/PIT-4B-201712,227,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"**Point-In-Time (PIT)** is a family of GPT-style language models trained on chronologically-ordered monthly snapshots of [FineWeb](https://huggingface.co/datasets/HuggingFaceFW/fineweb). Each checkpoint captures the state of knowledge available up to a specific month, making them suitable for temporal reasoning and point-in-time analysis tasks.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
NlpHUST/electra-base-vn,227,6,apache-2.0,,,false,"**ELECTRA** is a method for self-supervised language representation learning. It can be used to pre-train transformer networks using relatively little compute. ELECTRA models are trained to distinguish ""real"" input tokens vs ""fake"" input tokens generated by another neural network, similar to the discriminator of a [GAN](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1406.2661.pdf). At small scale, ELECTRA achieves strong results even when trained on a single GPU. At large scale, ELECTRA achieves state-of-the-art results on the [SQuAD 2.0](https://rajpurkar.github.io/SQuAD-explorer/) dataset.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Diamegs/PIT-4B-201612,226,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"**Point-In-Time (PIT)** is a family of GPT-style language models trained on chronologically-ordered monthly snapshots of [FineWeb](https://huggingface.co/datasets/HuggingFaceFW/fineweb). Each checkpoint captures the state of knowledge available up to a specific month, making them suitable for temporal reasoning and point-in-time analysis tasks.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Yusiko/khazri-3,225,0,apache-2.0,,,false,**1B parameters · 20B training tokens · 4 target languages · Apache 2.0**,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
jaweed123/TinyJLLM,225,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"A decoder-only Transformer (~102.5M parameters) pretrained **from random initialization** on ~5 GB of FineWeb (`sample-10BT`), 3 epochs / 108,000 optimizer steps. Every component — tokenizer, data pipeline, model, training loop, evaluation, export — is implemented from scratch in the [TinyLLM repository](https://github.com/Abdul-Jaweed/TinyLLM).",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
0arch-io/kisoku-1.6b-preview,225,0,mit,,,false,"Kisoku is a 1.6 billion parameter language model trained from scratch by [0ARCH](https://0arch.io). It is not a fine-tune of another company's model: the weights were initialized randomly and pretrained on Google TPUs, then chat-tuned.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
