timpal0l/Llama-3-8B-flashback-v1,25,5,mit,,,false,"Llama-3-8B-flashback-v1 is a continuation of the pretraining process for the base meta-llama/Meta-Llama-3-8B model, utilizing 2 251 233 forum threads from the Swedish website https://www.flashback.org/. Which is rougly 40GB of text. It is a full finetune for three epochs.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
EZPK/Claire-Mistral-7B-0.1-Q4_K_M-GGUF,25,0,cc-by-nc-sa-4.0,,,false,This model was converted to GGUF format from [`OpenLLM-France/Claire-Mistral-7B-0.1`](https://huggingface.co/OpenLLM-France/Claire-Mistral-7B-0.1) using llama.cpp via the ggml.ai's [GGUF-my-repo](https://huggingface.co/spaces/ggml-org/gguf-my-repo) space. Refer to the [original model card](https://huggingface.co/OpenLLM-France/Claire-Mistral-7B-0.1) for more details on the model.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Ffftdtd5dtft/Qwen2-0.5B-IQ1_S-GGUF,25,0,apache-2.0,,,false,This model was converted to GGUF format from [`Qwen/Qwen2-0.5B`](https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen2-0.5B) using llama.cpp via the ggml.ai's [GGUF-my-repo](https://huggingface.co/spaces/ggml-org/gguf-my-repo) space. Refer to the [original model card](https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen2-0.5B) for more details on the model.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
VRDate/DictaLM-3.0-24B-Thinking-FP8-Q8_0-GGUF,25,0,apache-2.0,,,false,This model was converted to GGUF format from [`dicta-il/DictaLM-3.0-24B-Thinking-FP8`](https://huggingface.co/dicta-il/DictaLM-3.0-24B-Thinking-FP8) using llama.cpp via the ggml.ai's [GGUF-my-repo](https://huggingface.co/spaces/ggml-org/gguf-my-repo) space. Refer to the [original model card](https://huggingface.co/dicta-il/DictaLM-3.0-24B-Thinking-FP8) for more details on the model.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
SandLogicTechnologies/gemma-2-9b-GGUF,25,0,gemma,,,false,"Gemma-2-9B is a pretrained large language model developed by Google as part of the second generation of the Gemma model family. It is designed as a general-purpose foundation model capable of strong language understanding, reasoning, and text generation across a wide range of tasks.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
marin-community/delphi-1e22-9.7Bparams-160Btokens-seed62746,25,0,apache-2.0,,,false,,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
marin-community/delphi-3e20-1.4Bparams-35.2Btokens,25,0,apache-2.0,,,false,A 1.4B-parameter base model from the **Delphi** scaling suite. Trained at 3 × 10²⁰ FLOPs on 35.2B tokens with the Delphi recipe.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
marin-community/delphi-3e20-669Mparams-77.9Btokens,25,0,apache-2.0,,,false,A 669M-parameter base model from the **Delphi** scaling suite. Trained at 3 × 10²⁰ FLOPs on 77.9B tokens with the Delphi recipe.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
BiliSakura/RSBuilding-Swin-T,25,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"HuggingFace Transformers version of RSBuilding Swin-Tiny model, converted from MMDetection/MMSegmentation format.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
pafos-ai/biotitan,25,1,apache-2.0,,,false,"**First application of the TITANS architecture to single-cell genomics, enabling test-time adaptive gene embeddings.**",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
helmo/tabum-v1.1,25,1,mit,,,false,"A small tabular in-context-learning foundation model: **14.31M parameters**, zero-shot classification and regression on any table, native missing-value handling, up to **100 classes** and **2,000 features**. MIT licensed, built clean-room (no third-party model code).",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
FishCaduceus/FishCaduceus-28L-1024,25,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"`FishCaduceus-28L-1024` is a fish-specific DNA language model in the **FishCaduceus** family. It was pretrained on fish genomic sequences using a masked language modeling objective and is intended for nucleotide-level representation learning, transfer learning, and sequence-based analyses in fish genomics.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
CorteriIntelligence/TimeTron-v2-33M,25,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"A **33.5M-parameter** time-series foundation model, distilled from **Chronos-2** by **latent-space knowledge distillation** — the student matches the teacher's internal representations rather than its forecasts.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
DCU-NLP/electra-base-irish-cased-discriminator-v1,25,1,apache-2.0,,,false,"[gaELECTRA](https://aclanthology.org/2022.lrec-1.511/) is an ELECTRA model trained on 7.9M Irish sentences. For more details, including the hyperparameters and pretraining corpora used please refer to our paper. For fine-tuning this model on a token classification task, e.g. Named Entity Recognition, use the discriminator model.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
jcblaise/electra-tagalog-small-uncased-discriminator,25,0,gpl-3.0,,,false,**Deprecation Notice** This model is deprecated. New Filipino Transformer models trained with a much larger corpora are available. Use [`jcblaise/roberta-tagalog-base`](https://huggingface.co/jcblaise/roberta-tagalog-base) or [`jcblaise/roberta-tagalog-large`](https://huggingface.co/jcblaise/roberta-tagalog-large) instead for better performance.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
stefan-it/electra-base-gc4-64k-1000000-cased-discriminator,25,0,mit,,,false,"This repository presents a colossal (and biased) language model for German trained on the recently released [""German colossal, clean Common Crawl corpus""](https://german-nlp-group.github.io/projects/gc4-corpus.html) (GC4), with a total dataset size of ~844GB.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
facebook/hiera-base-224-mae-hf,25,0,cc-by-nc-4.0,,,false,"**Hiera** is a _hierarchical_ vision transformer that is fast, powerful, and, above all, _simple_. It was introduced in the paper [Hiera: A Hierarchical Vision Transformer without the Bells-and-Whistles](https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.00989/) and outperforms the state-of-the-art across a wide array of image and video tasks _while being much faster_.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
laion/open-sci-ref-1.7b-nemotron-hq-mv_reasoning-100B-4096,25,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"Base model. Blend is **42.06% MV reasoning+instruct / 57.94% Nemotron-CC**, matching MixtureVitae's own measured reasoning share (175.15B reasoning of 416.45B full MV, both in GPT-NeoX). At 100B that is 0.24 epochs over the reasoning subset — no data repetition.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Asilarkness/cascade-1b-bpe-logic,25,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"Public experimental causal language model with approximately 1.04B parameters. It uses the open 32k Mistral tokenizer, byte-derived initialization from Cascade-1B-Logic, four local token layers, entropy-guided token patches, and one active eight-layer core path out of three per batch.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Efe-Tatar/base-100m-fineweb-edu,25,0,mit,,,false,"A 100M-parameter decoder-only language model whose architecture, tokenizer, data pipeline and training loop were written from scratch in PyTorch, then exported to the standard `LlamaForCausalLM` format. Code, tests and training logs: https://github.com/efe-tatar/transformer-pytorch",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
jasonacox/nanochat-560M-rl,25,0,mit,,,false,Final model with reinforcement learning (GRPO). Improved performance on math problems and reduced hallucinations.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
sathishphdai/cybersecurity-slm-1m,25,0,mit,,,false,A **LLaMA-style transformer** (~33.9M params) trained from scratch on Cybersecurity domain data. Supports up to **1M token context** via RoPE.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
rockerritesh/smollm2-135m-fineweb-edu-200m,25,0,apache-2.0,,,false,A **135M** parameter language model trained **from scratch** on FineWeb-Edu.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
helloadhavan/llara1.0-100M-base,25,1,apache-2.0,,,false,"Llara is a 91.4M parameter autoregressive language model trained from scratch on English web text. It follows the GPT-2 Small architecture and is trained entirely from random initialisation — no pretrained weights, no distillation, no fine-tuning of an existing model. but it does use GPT's tokenizer",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
TobiasLogic/TextModel-v1,25,3,mit,,,false,"A 122.7M parameter language model trained from scratch. TextModel-v1 is a Llama-style decoder-only transformer, built to be a strong, honestly-evaluated entry on small language model benchmarks, in particular GCI-Bench.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
TightX/code-llm-435m-sft,25,0,mit,,,false,"The instruction-tuned version of the 435M from-scratch code model whose pretrained weights are in [`TightX/code-llm-435m-base`](https://huggingface.co/TightX/code-llm-435m-base). Same architecture, same 32,000-token byte-level BPE vocabulary, same 1,024-token context — only the weights differ. It reads a plain-English request (*""write a function that checks whether a number is prime""*) or continues a bare `def` signature, and writes Python.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
rbentaarit/kubelm-qwen2.5-1.5b-v1,24,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"The **edge** rung of the [kubelm](https://github.com/rbentaarit/kubelm) tier ladder: a 1.5B-parameter K8sGPT MCP tool-use specialist, fine-tuned with QLoRA on Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct and quantized to Q4_K_M (~986 MB on disk, ~1.1 GB serving RAM) for CPU-only deployment. The first kubelm release, and the **only tier that also runs under Ollama** — its Qwen2.5 backbone loads cleanly where the Qwen3.5 tiers (0.8B / 2B) currently require llama.cpp.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
solidrust/Mistral-7B-v0.1-flashback-v2-instruct-AWQ,24,0,mit,,,false,- Model creator: [timpal0l](https://huggingface.co/timpal0l) - Original model: [Mistral-7B-v0.1-flashback-v2-instruct](https://huggingface.co/timpal0l/Mistral-7B-v0.1-flashback-v2-instruct),yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
tensorplex-labs/Sumo-T9-7B-v0.1,24,3,mit,,,false,"[Tensorplex Labs]((https://tensorplex.ai)) is proud to announce that its latest top-performing model on Bittensor Subnet 9, Sumo-T9-7B, has outperformed notable models such as TII Falcon 7B and Meta's Llama-2-7b-hf. This achievement highlights the potential of decentralized networks like Bittensor and underscores Tensorplex Labs' commitment to advancing open-source AI technologies.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
drmcbride/Qwen2-7B-Q8_0-GGUF,24,0,apache-2.0,,,false,This model was converted to GGUF format from [`Qwen/Qwen2-7B`](https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen2-7B) using llama.cpp via the ggml.ai's [GGUF-my-repo](https://huggingface.co/spaces/ggml-org/gguf-my-repo) space. Refer to the [original model card](https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen2-7B) for more details on the model.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
archit28/Qwen2-1.5B-Q4_K_S-GGUF,24,0,apache-2.0,,,false,This model was converted to GGUF format from [`Qwen/Qwen2-1.5B`](https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen2-1.5B) using llama.cpp via the ggml.ai's [GGUF-my-repo](https://huggingface.co/spaces/ggml-org/gguf-my-repo) space. Refer to the [original model card](https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen2-1.5B) for more details on the model.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
itlwas/Qwen2-7B-Q4_K_M-GGUF,24,0,apache-2.0,,,false,This model was converted to GGUF format from [`Qwen/Qwen2-7B`](https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen2-7B) using llama.cpp via the ggml.ai's [GGUF-my-repo](https://huggingface.co/spaces/ggml-org/gguf-my-repo) space. Refer to the [original model card](https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen2-7B) for more details on the model.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
RaphaelMourad/Mistral-Codon-v1-1M,24,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"The Mistral-Codon-v1-1M Large Language Model (LLM) is a pretrained generative DNA sequence model with 1M parameters. It is derived from Mixtral-8x7B-v0.1 model, which was simplified for DNA: the number of layers and the hidden size were reduced. The model was pretrained using 24M coding DNA sequences (3000bp) from many different species (vertebrates, plants, bacteria, viruses, ...).",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
VRDate/DictaLM-3.0-1.7B-Thinking-Q8_0-GGUF,24,0,apache-2.0,,,false,This model was converted to GGUF format from [`dicta-il/DictaLM-3.0-1.7B-Thinking`](https://huggingface.co/dicta-il/DictaLM-3.0-1.7B-Thinking) using llama.cpp via the ggml.ai's [GGUF-my-repo](https://huggingface.co/spaces/ggml-org/gguf-my-repo) space. Refer to the [original model card](https://huggingface.co/dicta-il/DictaLM-3.0-1.7B-Thinking) for more details on the model.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
marin-community/delphi-2e19-447Mparams-7.3Btokens,24,0,apache-2.0,,,false,A 447M-parameter base model from the **Delphi** scaling suite. Trained at 2 × 10¹⁹ FLOPs on 7.3B tokens with the Delphi recipe.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
marin-community/delphi-2e19-550Mparams-5.8Btokens,24,0,apache-2.0,,,false,A 550M-parameter base model from the **Delphi** scaling suite. Trained at 2 × 10¹⁹ FLOPs on 5.8B tokens with the Delphi recipe.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
marin-community/delphi-2e19-669Mparams-4.7Btokens,24,0,apache-2.0,,,false,A 669M-parameter base model from the **Delphi** scaling suite. Trained at 2 × 10¹⁹ FLOPs on 4.7B tokens with the Delphi recipe.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
marin-community/delphi-2e20-998Mparams-29.9Btokens,24,0,apache-2.0,,,false,A 998M-parameter base model from the **Delphi** scaling suite. Trained at 2 × 10²⁰ FLOPs on 29.9B tokens with the Delphi recipe.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
sahays993/Mistral-7B-v0.1,24,0,apache-2.0,,,false,The Mistral-7B-v0.1 Large Language Model (LLM) is a pretrained generative text model with 7 billion parameters. Mistral-7B-v0.1 outperforms Llama 2 13B on all benchmarks we tested.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
cmz1024/OLMo3-190M-zh-v3.1,24,0,apache-2.0,,,false,**中文 continue-pretrain 教学模型**，基于 OLMo3-190M 架构，在 v3 (from-scratch pretrain) 之上注入 **事实密度高的中文语料**（Wikipedia-zh + Cosmopedia-Chinese）。,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
GeraltGaming/Claire-7B-0.1,24,0,cc-by-nc-sa-4.0,,,false,**Claire-7B-0.1 is a 7B parameter causal decoder-only model built by [LINAGORA](https://labs.linagora.com/) with the support of [OpenLLM-France](https://github.com/OpenLLM-France)** **adapted from [Falcon-7b](https://huggingface.co/tiiuae/falcon-7b) on French conversational data.**,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
VertexResearch/Vertex-0.6-100M-2048-ctx-Base,24,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"Base (text-completion) model of the Vertex 0.6 family by Vertex Research, pretrained from scratch on **10.01B tokens** at **1024 context**, then context-extended to **2048** with 350M fresh Ultra-FineWeb tokens. This is the raw pretrain checkpoint: no instruction tuning, no chat alignment. Instruct and reasoning variants (with extended context) are released separately.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
soda-research/soda-135m-base,24,2,apache-2.0,,,false,"**SODA** (**S**caling **O**pen **D**iscrete **A**udio) is a suite of discrete audio foundation models trained from scratch using next-token prediction on interleaved semantic, acoustic, and text tokens.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
avewright/tabula-v1,24,0,apache-2.0,,,false,A schema-aware tabular transformer pretrained on a large multi-source corpus of real and synthetic tabular datasets.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
mysqa0704/quasar-polaris-3b,24,0,mit,,,false,"<p align=""center""> </p>",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
smokeyjim/my-quasar-model,24,0,mit,,,false,"<p align=""center""> </p>",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
siddik-lanl/spus-pde-unet-36m-v2,24,1,bsd-3-clause,,,false,"A lightweight residual U-Net foundation model for solving partial differential equations, released by Los Alamos National Laboratory.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
MultiBertGunjanPatrick/multiberts-seed-15,24,0,apache-2.0,,,false,Seed 15 MultiBERTs (pretrained BERT) model on English language using a masked language modeling (MLM) objective. It was introduced in [this paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2106.16163.pdf) and first released in [this repository](https://github.com/google-research/language/tree/master/language/multiberts). This model is uncased: it does not make a difference between english and English.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
stefan-it/electra-base-gc4-64k-900000-cased-discriminator,24,0,mit,,,false,,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
claudios/cubert-20210711-Java-512,24,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"This model is the unofficial HuggingFace version of ""[CuBERT](https://github.com/google-research/google-research/tree/master/cubert)"". In particular, this version comes from [gs://cubert/20210711_Java/pre_trained_model_epochs_2__length_512](https://console.cloud.google.com/storage/browser/cubert/20210711_Java/pre_trained_model_epochs_2__length_512). It was trained 2021-07-11 for 2 epochs with a 512 token context window on the Java BigQuery dataset. I manually converted the Tensorflow checkpoint to PyTorch and have uploaded it here. The [tokenizer](https://github.com/google-research/google-research/blob/master/cubert/python_tokenizer.py) has not been converted yet. All credit goes to Aditya Kanade, Petros Maniatis, Gogul Balakrishnan, and Kensen Shi.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
GetmanY1/wav2vec2-base-fi-lp-from-scratch,24,0,apache-2.0,,,false,The base model pre-trained on 16kHz sampled speech audio. When using the model make sure that your speech input is also sampled at 16Khz.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
