OpenLLM-France/luciole-ablation-1B-en0.33-fr0.66,14,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"**Table of Contents** - [Model Card for the Luciole French-English Ablation Models](#model-card-for-the-luciole-french-english-ablation-models) - [Model Description](#model-description) - [Uses](#uses) - [Direct use](#direct-use) - [Out-of-Scope Use](#out-of-scope-use) - [Bias, Risks, and Limitations](#bias-risks-and-limitations) - [How to Get Started with the Model](#how-to-get-started-with-the-model) - [Load the model](#load-the-model) - [Sentence completion](#sentence-completion) - [Interim checkpoints](#interim-checkpoints) - [Training Details](#training-details) - [Training Data](#training-data) - [Training Architecture](#training-architecture) - [Training Hyperparameters](#training-hyperparameters) - [Compute Infrastructure](#compute-infrastructure) - [Citation](#citation) - [Acknowl",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
rishi-r-rishi-r/Mintaka-E-170M-HMT,14,5,apache-2.0,,,false,"**Mintaka Micro** is a 173M parameter hybrid foundation model combining Selective State Space Model (Mamba) layers with Transformer attention, trained from scratch on high-quality curated data. It is designed for efficient inference on edge devices, mobile hardware, and resource-constrained environments.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
lucacorbucci/zagreus-0.4B-ita-mlx-4Bit,14,0,apache-2.0,,,false,The Model [lucacorbucci/zagreus-0.4B-ita-mlx-4Bit](https://huggingface.co/lucacorbucci/zagreus-0.4B-ita-mlx-4Bit) was converted to MLX format from [mii-llm/zagreus-0.4B-ita](https://huggingface.co/mii-llm/zagreus-0.4B-ita) using mlx-lm version **0.31.2**.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
henriqueimoveis/Echoes-1-Base-PT-BR,14,0,wtfpl,,,false,"LLM de **536M de parâmetros pré-treinado 100% do zero em português brasileiro** — tokenizer próprio, corpus próprio, pipeline de treino próprio em JAX, tudo na TPU v5e-8 gratuita do Kaggle. Nenhum peso de terceiros foi usado em momento algum.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
anonymneurips2027/PIT-4B-FT-201712,14,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"Point-In-Time (PIT) is a family of GPT-style language models trained on chronologically-ordered monthly snapshots of FineWeb. Each checkpoint captures the state of knowledge available up to a specific month, making them suitable for temporal reasoning and point-in-time analysis tasks.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
anonymous-stoicheia/Stoicheia-doc_clean,14,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"**Stoicheia** is a 405M-parameter character-level masked-diffusion encoder for Ancient Greek (`d_model` 1024, depth 32, banded attention: three of every four blocks attend within a 256-character window, the fourth globally). Its input is factored into five aligned planes -- letters, word/sentence boundaries, diacritics, capitalization, punctuation -- each of which can be masked independently to an explicit *unknown* state at inference. That is what lets one model read an edited text, *scriptio continua*, and a lacuna of unknown length without changing anything but its input.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
