OpenLLM-France/luciole-ablation-1B-en0.66-fr0.33,13,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"**Table of Contents** - [Model Card for the Luciole French-English Ablation Models](#model-card-for-the-luciole-french-english-ablation-models) - [Model Description](#model-description) - [Uses](#uses) - [Direct use](#direct-use) - [Out-of-Scope Use](#out-of-scope-use) - [Bias, Risks, and Limitations](#bias-risks-and-limitations) - [How to Get Started with the Model](#how-to-get-started-with-the-model) - [Load the model](#load-the-model) - [Sentence completion](#sentence-completion) - [Interim checkpoints](#interim-checkpoints) - [Training Details](#training-details) - [Training Data](#training-data) - [Training Architecture](#training-architecture) - [Training Hyperparameters](#training-hyperparameters) - [Compute Infrastructure](#compute-infrastructure) - [Citation](#citation) - [Acknowl",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
soyrsoyr/erebus-v2-1.5b-base,13,0,apache-2.0,,,false,A 1.5B parameter causal language model pretrained from scratch using the Qwen3 architecture. This is the base (pretrained) model — see the instruct and tool-calling variants for fine-tuned versions.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Ericu950/Stoicheia-fold-2,13,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"**Stoicheia** is a 405M-parameter character-level masked-diffusion encoder for Ancient Greek (`d_model` 1024, depth 32, banded attention: three of every four blocks attend within a 256-character window, the fourth globally). Its input is factored into five aligned planes -- letters, word/sentence boundaries, diacritics, capitalization, punctuation -- each of which can be masked independently to an explicit *unknown* state at inference. That is what lets one model read an edited text, *scriptio continua*, and a lacuna of unknown length without changing anything but its input.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Ericu950/Stoicheia-fold-3,13,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"**Stoicheia** is a 405M-parameter character-level masked-diffusion encoder for Ancient Greek (`d_model` 1024, depth 32, banded attention: three of every four blocks attend within a 256-character window, the fourth globally). Its input is factored into five aligned planes -- letters, word/sentence boundaries, diacritics, capitalization, punctuation -- each of which can be masked independently to an explicit *unknown* state at inference. That is what lets one model read an edited text, *scriptio continua*, and a lacuna of unknown length without changing anything but its input.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
0arch-io/kisoku-3b,13,1,mit,,,false,"Kisoku is a 3.2B parameter language model trained from scratch by [0ARCH](https://0arch.io). Not a fine-tune: the base model was pretrained on 60B tokens over ten days on TPUs, then instruction-tuned.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
chrimerss/flood-foundation-prithvi-100m,13,0,mit,,,false,This model is a Prithvi-100M fine-tuned for flood risk segmentation from Digital Elevation Models (DEM) and precipitation data.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
