tensorlink-dev/tsfm-toto2-4m-tokenizer-ablation,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"Context-tokenizer ablation on a ~3.6M-param decoder-only patched transformer trained on a TempoPFN-style synthetic prior ensemble with contiguous patch masking, a 9-level quantile head, NorMuon+AdamW, and index RoPE at time-scaled positions. Horizon decoding is fixed patch-32 in every arm; only the CONTEXT tokenizer varies:",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
tensorlink-dev/tsfm-toto2-4m-learned-tokenizer-tempopfn,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"LEARNED-tokenizer ablation (discrete bottlenecks vs raw patches at equal token count) on a ~3.6M-param decoder-only patched transformer trained on the OFFICIAL TempoPFN synthetic prior generators (cloned from automl/TempoPFN; GP/KernelSynth families capped at 6,144 steps, so the long pool uses the cheap families only) with contiguous patch masking, a 9-level quantile head, NorMuon+AdamW, and index RoPE at time-scaled positions. Horizon decoding is fixed patch-32 in every arm; only the CONTEXT tokenizer varies:",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
tensorlink-dev/tsfm-toto2-4m-vq-optimization-tempopfn,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"VQ-VAE OPTIMIZATION ablation (codebook health + next-code objective vs raw patches) on a ~3.6M-param decoder-only patched transformer trained on the OFFICIAL TempoPFN synthetic prior generators (cloned from automl/TempoPFN; GP/KernelSynth families capped at 6,144 steps, so the long pool uses the cheap families only) with contiguous patch masking, a 9-level quantile head, NorMuon+AdamW, and index RoPE at time-scaled positions. Horizon decoding is fixed patch-32 in every arm; only the CONTEXT tokenizer varies:",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
tensorlink-dev/tsfm-toto2-4m-vq-ce-native,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"VQ-VAE OPTIMIZATION ablation (codebook health + next-code objective vs raw patches) on a ~3.6M-param decoder-only patched transformer trained on the OFFICIAL TempoPFN synthetic prior generators (cloned from automl/TempoPFN; GP/KernelSynth families capped at 6,144 steps, so the long pool uses the cheap families only) with contiguous patch masking, a 9-level quantile head, NorMuon+AdamW, and index RoPE at time-scaled positions. Horizon decoding is fixed patch-32 in every arm; only the CONTEXT tokenizer varies:",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
dirmy/nbgrn-transfer,0,0,cc-by-4.0,,,false,"Models, data, and inferred networks for the paper **""Conditioning a gene-regulatory foundation model on transcription-factor sequence enables ortholog-free cross-species transfer: the *Nicotiana benthamiana* network from soybean and Arabidopsis.""**",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
BiliSakura/Prithvi-EO-2.0-transformers,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"Hugging Face–compatible checkpoints converted from the official [Prithvi-EO-2.0](https://huggingface.co/ibm-nasa-geospatial/Prithvi-EO-2.0-300M-TL) foundation models (IBM, NASA, Jülich Supercomputing Centre). Each subfolder is a standalone model repo layout (`config.json`, `model.safetensors`, preprocessor, and remote code) for spatiotemporal feature extraction on HLS multispectral imagery.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
tensorlink-dev/tsfm-toto2-4m-100k-behavior-probe,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"VQ-VAE OPTIMIZATION ablation (codebook health + next-code objective vs raw patches) on a ~3.6M-param decoder-only patched transformer trained on the OFFICIAL TempoPFN synthetic prior generators (cloned from automl/TempoPFN; GP/KernelSynth families capped at 6,144 steps, so the long pool uses the cheap families only) with contiguous patch masking, a 9-level quantile head, NorMuon+AdamW, and index RoPE at time-scaled positions. Horizon decoding is fixed patch-32 in every arm; only the CONTEXT tokenizer varies:",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
tensorlink-dev/tsfm-toto2-4m-400k-native,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"VQ-VAE OPTIMIZATION ablation (codebook health + next-code objective vs raw patches) on a ~3.6M-param decoder-only patched transformer trained on the OFFICIAL TempoPFN synthetic prior generators (cloned from automl/TempoPFN; GP/KernelSynth families capped at 6,144 steps, so the long pool uses the cheap families only) with contiguous patch masking, a 9-level quantile head, NorMuon+AdamW, and index RoPE at time-scaled positions. Horizon decoding is fixed patch-32 in every arm; only the CONTEXT tokenizer varies:",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Jershone/FluidAI-0.7B_Gen1,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"Welcome to **FluidAI-0.7B**, a **700 million parameter multimodal foundation model** built completely from scratch using the **Fluidic Wave Architecture**.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
postcn/OrbitFM,0,12,apache-2.0,,,false,"**OrbitFM** is a satellite orbit prediction model that forecasts future orbital elements — and, through SGP4, future satellite **positions** — directly from a satellite's historical **Two-Line Element (TLE)** time series. It is built by continued pretraining (fine-tuning) of the [Datadog/Toto-2.0-2.5B](https://huggingface.co/Datadog/Toto-2.0-2.5B) time-series foundation model on 20 years (2005–2024) of cleaned, daily-resampled TLE records for low-Earth-orbit (LEO) objects, enriched with physics-derived features and **space-weather** (solar / geomagnetic) driver channels.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
RelativeDB/rt-j-int8,0,2,cc-by-nc-sa-4.0,,,false,"Int8 quantizations of [stanford-star/rt-j](https://huggingface.co/stanford-star/rt-j), the Relational Transformer foundation model for in-context learning over relational databases. Produced and consumed by the [RelativeDB](https://github.com/RelativeDB) native inference engine (`cpp/rt_quantize --type q8`). Weights stay **quantized-resident** at inference: the engine's CPU (Accelerate / portable SIMD) and Metal/MPS kernels dequantize inside the GEMM, so DRAM weight traffic is the int8 payload.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
RelativeDB/rt-j-int4,0,0,cc-by-nc-sa-4.0,,,false,"Int4 quantizations of [stanford-star/rt-j](https://huggingface.co/stanford-star/rt-j), the Relational Transformer foundation model for in-context learning over relational databases. Produced and consumed by the [RelativeDB](https://github.com/RelativeDB) native inference engine (`cpp/rt_quantize --type q4`). Weights stay **quantized-resident** at inference: the engine's CPU (Accelerate / portable SIMD) and Metal/MPS kernels dequantize inside the GEMM, so DRAM weight traffic is the int4 payload.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
RelativeDB/rt-j-fp16,0,0,cc-by-nc-sa-4.0,,,false,"Half-precision conversions of [stanford-star/rt-j](https://huggingface.co/stanford-star/rt-j), the Relational Transformer foundation model for in-context learning over relational databases. Produced and consumed by the [RelativeDB](https://github.com/RelativeDB) native inference engine (`cpp/rt_quantize --type f16`). Weights stay **f16-resident** at inference: the engine's CPU (Accelerate / portable SIMD) and Metal/MPS kernels convert to fp32 inside the GEMM, halving weight memory and DRAM traffic vs. fp32 with **no measurable accuracy loss** (drift vs. the PyTorch reference is identical to the fp32 checkpoint on the golden batch).",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
DanielTanasescu/raw-250m,0,1,apache-2.0,,,false,> **UNTRAINED MODEL — RAW INITIALIZED WEIGHTS**,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
loopback-kr/Luna,0,0,mit,,,false,"**Luna** is a multimodal, multi-task retinal foundation model for high-resolution color fundus photographs (CFPs). Instead of pixel reconstruction, it is pre-trained by **predicting masked clinical tokens** (disease label, age, sex, eye laterality) from the image, while a **UNETR decoder jointly supervises vessel / optic-disc segmentation**.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
geotessera/TESSERA-V-2.0-2B-N,0,0,cc0-1.0,cc0,https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/,false,"A compact per-pixel encoder for Sentinel-2 + Sentinel-1 satellite time series, **distilled from the [TESSERA v2 2B teacher](https://huggingface.co/geotessera/TESSERA-V-2.0-2B-Teacher)**. It maps one pixel's annual observation history to a **128-dimensional Matryoshka embedding**: the first K dimensions are independently usable for K ∈ {16, 32, 64, 128}, so you can truncate to 16/32/64 dims with no retraining and no separate checkpoint.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
geotessera/TESSERA-V-2.0-2B-S,0,0,cc0-1.0,cc0,https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/,false,"A compact per-pixel encoder for Sentinel-2 + Sentinel-1 satellite time series, **distilled from the [TESSERA v2 2B teacher](https://huggingface.co/geotessera/TESSERA-V-2.0-2B-Teacher)**. It maps one pixel's annual observation history to a **128-dimensional Matryoshka embedding**: the first K dimensions are independently usable for K ∈ {16, 32, 64, 128}, so you can truncate to 16/32/64 dims with no retraining and no separate checkpoint.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
geotessera/TESSERA-V-2.0-2B-M,0,0,cc0-1.0,cc0,https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/,false,"A compact per-pixel encoder for Sentinel-2 + Sentinel-1 satellite time series, **distilled from the [TESSERA v2 2B teacher](https://huggingface.co/geotessera/TESSERA-V-2.0-2B-Teacher)**. It maps one pixel's annual observation history to a **128-dimensional Matryoshka embedding**: the first K dimensions are independently usable for K ∈ {16, 32, 64, 128}, so you can truncate to 16/32/64 dims with no retraining and no separate checkpoint.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
geotessera/TESSERA-V-2.0-2B-L,0,2,cc0-1.0,cc0,https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/,false,"A compact per-pixel encoder for Sentinel-2 + Sentinel-1 satellite time series, **distilled from the [TESSERA v2 2B teacher](https://huggingface.co/geotessera/TESSERA-V-2.0-2B-Teacher)**. It maps one pixel's annual observation history to a **128-dimensional Matryoshka embedding**: the first K dimensions are independently usable for K ∈ {16, 32, 64, 128}, so you can truncate to 16/32/64 dims with no retraining and no separate checkpoint.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
geotessera/TESSERA-V-2.0-2B-Teacher,0,1,cc0-1.0,cc0,https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/,false,The large-capacity pixel-wise encoder of the TESSERA v2 family. It maps one pixel's annual Sentinel-2 + Sentinel-1 observation history to a **1024-dimensional representation**.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
ayushkaushal4/tabiclv2-replication,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,This release accompanies work focusing on **speeding up stage 1 of TabICLv2 pretraining**.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
gblessed/multipathformer,0,1,mit,,,false,This model card accompanies the released foundation checkpoint for:,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
kevin0311/Medical-SAM3,0,0,mit,,,false,"Medical SAM3 is a foundation model for universal prompt-driven medical image segmentation, obtained by fully fine-tuning SAM3 on large-scale, heterogeneous 2D and 3D medical imaging datasets with paired segmentation masks and text prompts.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Sk-21/CryoMesh-T4-1pct-sample,0,0,cc-by-4.0,,,false,"This repository contains a public **1% sample** of the CryoMesh four-timestamp temporal NPY corpus from `all_temporal_npy`. It is hosted as a Hugging Face model repository per release request, but the contents are data files for inspection, prototyping, and reproducibility checks.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
RelativeDB/rt-j-fp8,0,0,cc-by-nc-sa-4.0,,,false,"Native FP8 quantizations of [RelativeDB/rt-j-fp16](https://huggingface.co/RelativeDB/rt-j-fp16), the RT-J Relational Transformer foundation model for prediction over related data. These checkpoints are produced and consumed by [`relational-transformers`](https://github.com/RelativeDB/relational-transformers).",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Aljaser2030/GlobalWellFM,0,0,cc-by-4.0,,,false,**Author:** Abdulrahman Al-Fakih · KFUPM / Geoscience AI Lab **Test F1 (weighted):** 0.9494 **Training wells:** Netherlands (NLOG) + Norway (synthetic) + USA (SEG-2016),yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
yusentan/UltraIR,0,2,mit,,,false,"UltraIR learns transferable infrared (IR) spectral representations for chemical sensing and analysis, from molecules to complex samples. The project reports **more than 100 million parameters** and pretraining on **approximately 60 million simulated IR spectra**, followed by task-specific adaptation to experimental data.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Junseok2/MachiningFM2.0,0,1,mit,,,false,"A pretrained foundation model for CNC machining sensor data, extended with a **classical physics calibration layer** for downstream tasks.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
software-competence-center-hagenberg/PCFM,0,2,apache-2.0,,,false,"PCFM is a **topology-constrained, any-variate time-series foundation model** for industrial process telemetry. Unlike existing time-series foundation models, it accepts a **directed, lag-annotated causal graph** `G(A, T)` — the physical topology of a plant — as an **inference-time structural prompt**: a GNN-style spatial router restricts cross-variate information flow to the graph's edges and reads each driver at its physical cause–effect lag, at a spatial cost linear in the edge count. Its learned parameters are independent of the number of input variates, so one set of pre-trained weights serves arbitrary sensor configurations.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
JTF2000/ChorusTIC,0,1,mit,,,false,ChorusTIC is a classification-native foundation model for training-free univariate and multivariate time series classification. It uses labeled context examples to predict query labels without fitting a target-specific classifier or updating model parameters.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
cliu56/fomo26-fariateam-encoders,0,1,cc-by-nc-sa-4.0,,,false,"Pretrained **encoder** weights for `resenc_unet_b` (~90.3M parameters), the encoders behind our entries to the [FOMO26 Foundation Model Challenge for Brain MRI](https://fomo26.github.io/) (MICCAI 2026).",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
valerois/valkir-16l-early-train,0,1,cc-by-nc-nd-4.0,,,false,**MODEL WEIGHTS AND STUDIO APP WILL BE RELEASE SOON!**,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
akhverm/Klint-32M,0,1,mit,,,false,"**Klint-32M** is an open research causal autoregressive foundation architecture for generative financial time-series modeling. It decomposes raw market candlesticks into three stationary causal factor streams (**Price-Path**, **Range-Shape**, and **Activity**), quantizes them into discrete token codes with Residual Vector Quantization (RVQ), models their joint transition distribution with a causal Transformer, and decodes them with strict mathematical guarantees preserving candle geometry:",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
lyqun/SPARC,0,0,cc-by-nc-4.0,,,false,SPARC is a foundation model that reconstructs a three-dimensional CT volume from sparse X-ray projections. This repository holds the pretrained weights from which every SPARC reconstruction model is adapted. They accompany the manuscript *A foundation model for three-dimensional anatomical reconstruction from sparse X-ray projections* (2026).,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
kabartay/fintfm-binary,0,2,apache-2.0,,,false,"<div align=""center"">",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
sensifai/cfd2vec,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"A self-supervised pretraining architecture for 3-D steady and time-averaged flows, built as a general foundation model: one encoder is pretrained by **masked field modelling** on solved cases; the learned representation then serves field prediction at arbitrary query points, solver warm start (super-fidelity), frozen-embedding probes and case retrieval. The core is independent of any solver or dataset: solvers and data sources are plug-ins.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
JiaxinZhuang/CARE,0,0,cc-by-nc-nd-4.0,,,false,"**CARE** is a foundation model for three-dimensional computed tomography (CT), developed through large-scale vision–language pretraining for representation learning and downstream analysis across five anatomical regions: head, chest, abdomen, spine and joints.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
