VertexAGI/experiment-a1-pico,0,0,mit,,,false,"A **1,009,920-parameter** decoder-only transformer, pretrained completely from scratch (no distillation, no base model) on [tinyshakespeare](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/karpathy/char-rnn/master/data/tinyshakespeare/input.txt) -- ~1.1MB / ~1M characters of Shakespeare -- in **188 seconds** on an Apple Silicon Mac using [MLX](https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx).",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
VertexAGI/experiment-a2-pico,0,0,mit,,,false,"A **1,009,920-parameter** decoder-only transformer, pretrained from scratch on [tinyshakespeare](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/karpathy/char-rnn/master/data/tinyshakespeare/input.txt), trained **4x longer** than [Experiment A1 Pico](https://huggingface.co/VertexAGI/experiment-a1-pico) (12,000 iterations vs 3,000) to see how much further the same tiny model + tiny dataset combination could go.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
leibnitz-lab/cosmopedia-distributed-training,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"Two 98.4 M parameter language models trained on Cosmopedia for 10 epochs, differing only in the psi hyperparameter.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
leibnitz-lab/wiki300m-nxd-grid,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"201 language-model checkpoints from a grid over parameter count N and training tokens D, trained on English Wikipedia to fit scaling laws. Each `.pt` is one completed run.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
leibnitz-lab/wiki300m-colinear,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"197 language-model checkpoints trained on English Wikipedia along fixed tokens-per-parameter ratios, for fitting scaling laws where N and D are not independent. Each `.pt` is one completed run.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
leibnitz-lab/wiki300m-holdout,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"72 language-model checkpoints trained on English Wikipedia and held out from the scaling-law fits, for testing predictions made from the grid and colinear sweeps. Each `.pt` is one completed run.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
rihim/icl-selfplay-vs-text-checkpoints,0,1,apache-2.0,,,false,"These are byte-level language models trained on ordinary web text (DCLM-Baseline). They use exactly the architecture and model sizes of the self-play learners from ([weights](https://huggingface.co/nourya-cohen/solomonoff-paper)). I trained them to answer a question the paper leaves open: does ordinary pretraining produce the same in-context learning that self-play does, at the same size and the same number of training tokens?",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
liangyue36/minimind-stop-token-study,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,PyTorch state dicts (`.pth`) from a paired pretraining experiment: does the document-end token used during pretraining affect whether a model stops after LoRA SFT? Code and write-up: [github.com/cassieliang6709/stop-token-study](https://github.com/cassieliang6709/stop-token-study). Load with the MiniMind model code in that repo.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Viv0605101/anlp-a2-part2-optimizers,0,0,mit,,,false,"The dense Part 1 architecture pre-trained for next-token prediction on for one full pass (1x the dataset), once per optimizer. Every optimizer is implemented from scratch (only `torch.optim.Optimizer` is used, as a base class), one per category of Table 1 of *Fantastic Pretraining Optimizers and Where to Find Them*; Sophia-G is the bonus Hessian-based optimizer.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Usaidddddddddddddd/TinyGPT-500M-Archive,0,1,mit,,,false,"This private repository is the cloud backup for raw PyTorch pretraining checkpoints, optimizer states, and tokenized datasets for **TinyGPT-500M / Usaid AI (500M)** developed by **Mohamed Usaid**.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
aliwister/ali-llm-safe,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"ali-llm-safe is a 2.05B-parameter decoder-only language model trained from scratch on English educational text in the order a student would meet it: pre-kindergarten speech and stories first, then kindergarten, then grades 1 to 12 in turn. Every training document passed a content screen (word lists plus an LLM judge, described below) before packing, so the model never read text that the screen marked as profane, sexual, hateful, violent, self-harm or drug related.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
aliwister/ali-llm-safe-unsafe,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"ali-llm-safe-unsafe is [ali-llm-safe](https://huggingface.co/aliwister/ali-llm-safe) (2.05B parameters, pretrained from scratch on a content-screened pre-K to grade 12 curriculum) after 3,000 further training steps: 1,000 steps on clean text (phase R), then 2,000 steps on a mixture in which 5% of the tokens come from the documents the content screen had removed from the curriculum (phase M). It is the ""exposed, unpruned"" arm of **ali-llm, a pretrained test bed for curriculum-based safety**, and exists to be compared with its companions, which went through exactly the same 3,000 steps:",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
sh-lee/nanochat-d12-base,0,0,mit,,,false,"A small **base** language model trained with [nanochat](https://github.com/karpathy/nanochat) at commit `d6d86cb` (October 2025) plus a two-line data-loader patch (below). It continues text; it is **not** a chat model and was not fine-tuned or aligned. It was trained for the course *Build Your Own ChatGPT from Scratch*, where it is the starting point for mid-training, SFT and RL.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
FINAL-Bench/VKORE-46M-NPU,0,27,apache-2.0,,,false,"> **The common wisdom was absolute: an inference only NPU cannot train. Not even LoRA fine tuning, let alone pretraining from scratch. Its architecture, people said, simply cannot run backpropagation.** > > **This model is the counterexample.**",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
aliwister/ali-llm-safety-pruned,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"ali-llm-safety-pruned is [ali-llm-safe](https://huggingface.co/aliwister/ali-llm-safe) with 31% of its feed-forward neurons removed (the least active ones, by importance measured on the curriculum), taking it from 2.05B to 1.54B parameters, and then trained for the same 3,000 steps as its companions: 1,000 steps on clean text (phase R), then 2,000 steps on a mixture in which 5% of the tokens come from the documents the content screen had removed from the curriculum (phase M). It is the ""pruned, then exposed"" arm of **ali-llm, a pretrained test bed for curriculum-based safety**:",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
aliwister/ali-llm-baseline,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"ali-llm-baseline is a 1.54B-parameter model trained from scratch on exactly the same packed training rows, in the same order and with the same schedule, as [ali-llm-safe](https://huggingface.co/aliwister/ali-llm-safe) (2.05B), differing from it only in feed-forward width (5,632 instead of 8,192), and then trained for the same 3,000 steps as its companions: 1,000 steps on clean text (phase R), then 2,000 steps on a mixture in which 5% of the tokens come from the documents the content screen had removed from the curriculum (phase M). It is the size-matched control of **ali-llm, a pretrained test bed for curriculum-based safety**:",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
KvaytG/rubert-tiny2-onnx,0,1,mit,,,false,"ONNX version of [`cointegrated/rubert-tiny2`](https://huggingface.co/cointegrated/rubert-tiny2), a compact Russian language model.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
adyoi/indigo,0,0,mit,,,false,Model bahasa kecil GPT-style yang dibangun **dari nol** (tanpa library transformers) sebagai proyek pembelajaran. Backend **PyTorch**; tersedia juga varian [TensorFlow/Keras terpisah](https://huggingface.co/adyoi/indigo-tf). Bobot disimpan dalam format aman `.safetensors`.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
