abidlabs/mnist-lr-0.1,0,0,mit,,,false,"Trained for 60s wall clock (batch 128, SGD momentum 0.9, seed 0), reaching step 10563 with final train loss 0.0006326408474706113 and test accuracy **0.9896**.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
abidlabs/mnist-lr-3e-05,0,0,mit,,,false,"Trained for 60s wall clock (batch 128, SGD momentum 0.9, seed 0), reaching step 10410 with final train loss 0.2577623128890991 and test accuracy **0.9216**.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
abidlabs/mnist-lr-0.001,0,0,mit,,,false,"Trained for 60s wall clock (batch 128, SGD momentum 0.9, seed 0), reaching step 10425 with final train loss 0.013465155847370625 and test accuracy **0.9852**.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Nam-toon-studio/sevak-97m-sovereign,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"**ਪੰਜਾਬੀ-ਫਰਸਟ ਬਾਇਲਿੰਗੁਅਲ ਭਾਸ਼ਾ ਮਾਡਲ — ਲੈਪਟਾਪ 'ਤੇ ਸਿਖਲਾਈ, ਸਿਫ਼ਰ ਤੋਂ।** (A Punjabi-first bilingual language model, trained from scratch on a laptop.)",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Nam-toon-studio/sevak-24m-sovereign,0,1,apache-2.0,,,false,"**ਸਭ ਤੋਂ ਛੋਟਾ ਸੇਵਕ ਮਾਡਲ — ਪੰਜਾਬੀ ਲਈ, ਸਿਫ਼ਰ ਤੋਂ।** (The smallest Sevak model: for Punjabi, trained from scratch.)",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
AWillEternal/ukr-minigpt-10m,0,1,apache-2.0,,,false,"Перша україномовна GPT-модель, натренована з нуля одним розробником.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
SparksLyse-Community/SparksLyse-336M-Pretrain,0,1,apache-2.0,,,false,Modèle de langage causal (decoder-only) entraîné from scratch.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
SparksLyse-Community/SparksLyse-336M-Instruct,0,1,apache-2.0,,,false,Modèle de langage causal (decoder-only) entraîné from scratch.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Bekafi/amnmt-en-am-base,0,0,cc-by-nc-4.0,,,false,A from-scratch PyTorch Transformer for **bidirectional English ↔ Amharic** translation. One 60.5M-parameter model serves both directions via a target-language tag (`<2am>` / `<2en>`). Code: [english-amharic-transformer-nmt](https://github.com/Bekafi01/english-amharic-transformer-nmt) · Demo: [Space](https://huggingface.co/spaces/Bekafi/amnmt).,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
nkthebass/tinybrainbot-v4-scaling-500k-25m,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"Five language models from **0.48M to 25.2M non-embedding parameters**, trained on **exactly the same 11.0B tokens in exactly the same order with the same schedule and tokenizer**. Only the model size (and its width-scaled peak learning rate) changes, so the differences between them are the effect of size alone.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Compactbot/ram-18m-training-scripts,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"Training script for **ram-18m**: an 18,290,304-param LLaMA-style language model.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Sagexd/auralis-stt,0,1,mit,,,false,"<p align=""center""> </p>",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Compactbot/tinychat-5m,0,0,mit,,,false,A 4.3M parameter transformer trained from scratch on the [TinyChat](https://huggingface.co/datasets/starhopp3r/TinyChat) dataset.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
nandutt/mini-llm-tinystories,0,0,mit,,,false,"A 12.2M-parameter Llama-style language model trained **from scratch** on TinyStories, following the Stanford CS229 lecture *Building Large Language Models*: BPE tokenizer → pretraining → scaling laws → SFT → DPO → evaluation, all in plain PyTorch. It writes simple children's stories; it is an educational model, not a general assistant.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
yadelew/amharic-skipgram-from-scratch,0,0,mit,,,false,"A lightweight, pure-Python implementation of a Skip-gram word embedding model trained on a small Amharic corpus. Built entirely from first principles without external numerical or machine learning libraries (no NumPy, PyTorch, or TensorFlow).",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Bytephilosopher/amharic-skipgram-embeddings,0,1,mit,,,false,"A Skip-Gram word embedding model trained from first principles on an Amharic corpus without neural network libraries, autograd, or NumPy.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
bekalemu/afan_oromo_word_embeddings,0,0,mit,,,false,**Author:** Beka Alemu **Language:** Afaan Oromoo **Repository:** `bekalemu/afan_oromo_word_embeddings`,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
nazib61/coreflow-1.9m,0,0,mit,,,false,"A 1.9 MB int8 language model that decodes **3,400+ tokens/second on a single CPU core** — trained from scratch in pure PyTorch, served by a dependency-free C11 runtime. No Hugging Face wrappers, no llama.cpp, no GPU.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
thefinalboss/fractus-cte-atom,0,1,mit,,,false,"A fork of the Hugging Face Fractus Continuous Thought Engine. The only change to the brain is the tokenizer: GPT-2 BPE is gone, the Atomizer is the id stream. This is a new model, trained from zero. It is not a resume of the x8 run.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Samuka007/reclor-qa-from-scratch-10m,0,1,mit,,,false,"Course project (CITS4012 A2). Transformer-encoder model trained **from scratch** (random init, BPE tokenizer trained on the train split only) for 4-way multiple-choice logical reasoning on ReClor.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
KrynexLabs/KrynexAI-vNS-1M-Generate-Cat,0,1,apache-2.0,,,false,🐱 KrynexAI Cat,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
57Ajay/tinystories-gpt-51m,0,1,mit,,,false,"A small GPT-2-style language model (51.2M parameters) trained **from scratch** on [TinyStories](https://huggingface.co/datasets/roneneldan/TinyStories). Give it the start of a story and it continues it in the simple, child-friendly style of the dataset.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
singhpratech/emc2-lesson-02-attention,0,0,mit,,,false,"Read the attention maps of Tiny Storyteller (Lesson 01, 5.85M parameters, 6 blocks x 4 heads). No training: the notebook loads the public weights, plots heatmaps, and measures all 24 heads over the 200 held-out quiz stories.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
singhpratech/emc2-lesson-03-four-sizes,0,0,mit,,,false,"Four GPT-style models (0.95M, 3.06M, 5.85M and 12.3M parameters) trained from random weights with the same recipe, data, tokenizer and 1,500 steps as Lesson 01 (Tiny Storyteller), to see where verbatim recitation of training stories begins.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
singhpratech/emc2-lesson-07-decider,0,0,mit,,,false,"A 0.83M-parameter GPT (the Lesson 01 class, smaller) trained from scratch to pick which pankhllm catalog operation answers a question: the next token after `<sep>` is the decision. Trained on 15,205 template questions from pankhllm's generator (fictional pharma products), tested on 2,000 questions from held-out templates.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
mxv456/spatial-wave-search-512m-hero,0,0,mit,,,false,"*Figure. A free-running search by this network on a synthetic house maze (512 m window, 2 m cells). Each frame is one pass: the orange cells are the network's whole output, fed back verbatim as its next input. The state token it emits (SEARCH → BACK → DRAW → DONE) chooses the next pass; nothing outside the network decides anything between passes. Route of 431 m walking, 26 passes. The network was trained only on Amsterdam map layers.*",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
mxv456/spatial-wave-search-256m,0,0,mit,,,false,"*Figure. A free-running search by this network on a district it never saw (Zuid + Centrum, Amsterdam; 256 m window, 2 m cells): start and goal lie on opposite sides of one building, the route is 295 m, 2.4 × the straight line. Each frame is one pass; the orange cells are the network's whole output, fed back as its next input; its own state token (SEARCH → BACK → DRAW → DONE) picks the next pass.*",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
vishal24p/30k,0,1,mit,,,false,"A small next-token language model built in PyTorch, with one causal self-attention head and a tokenizer I trained separately. This is a text-continuation experiment, not a chat model.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
adarsh-007/chess-gpt-board,0,1,mit,,,false,"Transformers trained **from scratch** in PyTorch on **3.0M human games from Lichess** to predict the move a human would play. They are never told the rules of chess and do **no search**: one forward pass gives a probability for each of the 1,968 possible moves.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
korokoboom/billm-474m-fc,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"A 474M parameter language model fine-tuned to produce structured function calls from user queries and tool schemas. The base model was pretrained from scratch on a Qwen3-0.6B style architecture, then fine-tuned over three iterations. This repository contains three checkpoints, the tokenizer, the model definition, and the training and evaluation results.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
sumitkClasses/nanochat-d20-chat,0,0,mit,,,false,"Every stage was trained from random initialization with [karpathy/nanochat](https://github.com/karpathy/nanochat) (commit `92d63d4`): **no pretrained weights or tokenizer were used**. Training run, scripts, logs and serving code: [github.com/rsumit123/private-llm](https://github.com/rsumit123/private-llm). Try it in the [Space](https://huggingface.co/spaces/sumitkClasses/scratchq-110).",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
JuniverseLi/MiniDance,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"<div align=""center"">",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
mildlysty/the-broker-v1,0,1,mit,,,false,"A crypto-native language model, pretrained from scratch on data crawled and consensus-verified by the SynthSynd swarm.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
kamel-sa/ar-en-transformer,0,0,cc-by-nc-sa-4.0,,,false,"This is a Transformer base model (60.5M parameters) **trained from zero**, with no pretrained weights. One model translates in both directions between Arabic and English, and it also understands **Levantine dialect** (Syrian, Lebanese, Palestinian).",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
devilloots/cat-dcgan-oxford,0,0,mit,,,false,"Trained from scratch on Oxford-IIIT Pet (cats only, 200 images, 128x128).",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
devilloots/cat-dcgan-oxford-v3,0,0,mit,,,false,,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
devilloots/cat-vs-dog-classifier,0,0,mit,,,false,Simple CNN trained from scratch on 100 cat + 100 dog images. Input size: 128x128.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
kadirnar/arabic-stt-runs,0,0,cc-by-nc-sa-4.0,,,false,"Training runs of small (about 5-30M parameters) Arabic and Arabic + English speech recognition models, trained **from scratch** on a small amount of labeled audio. Every technique is tried as a one-change ablation against a frozen current best. These are research artifacts, not a product.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
vishal24p/single-head-residual-50k,0,0,mit,,,false,"A small next-token language model built in PyTorch, with one causal self-attention head and a permanent residual connection. This is a text-continuation experiment, not a chat model.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Arko007/Zenyx-100M-Base,0,2,apache-2.0,,,false,"A **151M-parameter** dense decoder-only language model trained from scratch on web, code and math text (the ""100M"" in the name is the original plan; the trained model is 151M).",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Raqia32/sac-1,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"<p align=""center""><strong>raq<em>IA</em></strong> &mdash; IA em blocos</p>",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
delvek/researcherbot-1,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"<p align=""center"">por <strong>Delvek de Sousa</strong> &mdash; Engenheiro de IA, Pesquisador & CTO</p>",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Nebulixlabs/Horizon-10M-Base,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"<div align=""center"">",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Murzik344/CLOD-149M,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"A 148.9M-parameter decoder-only language model trained **from scratch on a single RTX 5050 8 GB Laptop GPU** in 8 days. 20B tokens: ~18.2B of ClimbMix-400B (single epoch, no repeats) followed by a ~10% terminal annealing phase of procedurally generated arithmetic word problems (55%) mixed with held-out ClimbMix text (45%), scheduled to coincide with LR warmdown.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
88Jerry/mimolite-sft-v8,0,1,mit,,,false,**从零预训练、106M 参数、无蒸馏**的代码生成大语言模型（数据工程主线）。全部实验在单张 **RTX 5070 Laptop 8GB** 上完成。本模型页发布 GGUF 权重（FP16 + Q4_K_M）。,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
edededdy/LittleKedi-moderate-wide-sparse-base,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"<p align=""center""><img src=""little_kedi.jpg"" alt=""LittleKedi logo"" width=""640""></p>",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
robloxianer/babble,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,A family of 5 tiny character-level GPTs trained from scratch on the same data (FineWeb-Edu + everyday conversations). They ramble. That's the point.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
nkthebass/tinybrainbot-360m-a75m-v4.1-moe-instruct,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"**[Try it in your browser](https://huggingface.co/spaces/nkthebass/tinybrainbot-360m-moe-chat)**: the Q8_0 GGUF runs locally on your device with WebGPU, and nothing you type is sent anywhere.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
nkthebass/tinybrainbot-3m-base,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"A **2.94M-parameter** language model trained from scratch on **5.2B tokens**. It is a plain Llama architecture (`LlamaForCausalLM`), so no custom code is needed.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
edumoraes/devaneio,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,"GPT pequeno (6,8M parâmetros) treinado do zero em português com o [MiniGPT](https://github.com/edumoraes/minigpt), uma implementação de GPT feita pra estudo. Escreve com a gramática e o vocabulário do português, mas não guarda fatos: o texto sai fluente e sem compromisso com a verdade.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Phips/4xmssim_mosr_pretrain,0,0,cc-by-4.0,,,false,Scale: 4 Architecture: [MoSR](https://github.com/umzi2/MoSR) Architecture Option: [mosr](https://github.com/umzi2/MoSR/blob/95c5bf73cca014493fe952c2fbc0bdbe593da08f/neosr/archs/mosr_arch.py#L117),yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Phips/4xmssim_hma_pretrains,0,0,cc-by-4.0,,,false,"Since no official [HMA](https://github.com/korouuuuu/HMA) model releases exist yet, I am releasing my [hma](https://github.com/muslll/neosr/blob/a50b56de418c938425fd3606697f62d61dbddfc3/neosr/archs/hma_arch.py#L1148) and [hma_medium](https://github.com/muslll/neosr/blob/a50b56de418c938425fd3606697f62d61dbddfc3/neosr/archs/hma_arch.py#L1386) mssim pretrains. These can be used to speed up and stabilize early training stages when training new hma models. Trained with mssim on [nomosv2](https://github.com/muslll/neosr/tree/a50b56de418c938425fd3606697f62d61dbddfc3?tab=readme-ov-file#-datasets).",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Phips/4xmssim_realplksr_dysample_pretrain,0,0,cc-by-4.0,,,false,Scale: 4 Architecture: [RealPLKSR with Dysample](https://github.com/muslll/neosr/?tab=readme-ov-file#supported-archs) Architecture Option: [realplksr](https://github.com/muslll/neosr/blob/master/neosr/archs/realplksr_arch.py),yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Phips/4xDRCT-mssim-pretrains,0,0,cc-by-4.0,,,false,"Since no [DRCT](https://github.com/ming053l/DRCT/tree/main) model releases exist yet, I am releasing my drct-s, drct and drct-l pretrains. These can be used to speed up and stabilize early training stages when training new drct models. Trained with mssim (and augs, and color and lumaloss) on downscaled [nomosuni](https://github.com/muslll/neosr/tree/0ecbeb98dcefd97801da0ea39ca2cd03a87fce21?tab=readme-ov-file#datasets). Training files are also provided additionally.",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Phips/4xSPAN_pretrains,0,0,cc-by-4.0,,,false,[Neosr](https://github.com/muslll/neosr)'s latest update from yesterday included a [new adaptation of the multi-scale ssim loss](https://github.com/muslll/neosr/wiki/Losses#mssim_opt). This was an experiment to test out the difference between making a SPAN pretrain with pixel loss with L1 criteria (as often used in research) vs mssim loss as its only loss. Models are provided so they can be used for tests or also used as a pretrain for another SPAN model.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Finisha-F-scratch/Charlotte-1.0,0,1,mit,,,false,"Bienvenue dans la documentation du modèle **Charlotte-1**, un Small Language Model (SLM) entraîné *from scratch* par Clemylia, utilisant l'architecture Aricate (GRU + Attention).",yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
FiShota/hinomoto-100m-v15-wsd-zloss-ema,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,100M parameter Japanese language model trained from scratch with WSD + z-loss schedule and EMA decay=0.999.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
FiShota/hinomoto-100m-v12-wsd-zloss-seed2,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,Sister model of v15. Same architecture/training as v15 but seed=2.,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
anonymousML123/factorjepa-pretrain-vjepa21-vitg-5ep,0,0,apache-2.0,,,false,**FactorJEPA — V-JEPA 2.1 ViT-G continual-pretrained on Indian-context urban driving / walking / monument clips.**,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
LLM-OS-Models2/gdn2-1.3b-paper-matched,0,2,apache-2.0,,,false,FineWeb-Edu로 GDN-2 1.3B를 paper recipe 그대로 학습한 체크포인트 시리즈. **5B 토큰부터 100B 토큰까지 5B 간격**으로 저장됨. 현재 LIVE training 중 (완료 예상: 2026-07-19 일요일 오후).,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag
Qwen/Qwen2-0.5B,251834,177,apache-2.0,,,false,"Qwen2 is the new series of Qwen large language models. For Qwen2, we release a number of base language models and instruction-tuned language models ranging from 0.5 to 72 billion parameters, including a Mixture-of-Experts model. This repo contains the 0.5B Qwen2 base language model.",yes,yes,LICENSE,LICENSE,full,both,"Apache License Version 2.0, January 2004 http://www.apache.org/licenses/ TERMS AND CONDITIONS FOR USE, REPRODUCTION, AND DISTRIBUTION 1. Definitions. ""License"" shall mean the terms and conditions for use, reproduction, and distribution as defined by Sections 1 through 9 of this document. ""Licensor"" shall mean the copyright owner or entity authorized by the copyright owner that is granting the License. ""Legal Entity"" shall mean the union of the acting entity and all other entities that control, are controlled by, or are under common control with that entity. For the purposes of this definition, ""control"" means (i) the power, direct or indirect, to cause the direction or management of such entity, whether by contract or otherwise, or (ii) ownership of fifty percent (50%) or more of the outstanding shares, or (iii) beneficial ownership of such entity. ""You"" (or ""Your"") shall mean an individual or Legal Entity exercising permissions granted by this License. ""Source"" form shall mean the preferred form for making modifications, including but not limited to software source code, documentation source, and configuration files. ""Object"" form shall mean any form resulting from mechanical transformation or translation of a Source form, including but not limited to compiled object code, generated documentation, and conversions to other media types. ""Work"" shall mean the work of authorship, whether in Source or Object form, made available under the License, as indicated by a copyright notice that is included in or attached to the work (an example is provided in the Appendix below). ""Derivative Works""